  "structure": {
    "block_count": 60,
    "blocks": [
      {
        "block_id": "block_000000",
        "block_index": 0,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h1",
        "text": "12 Home Remedies for Pregnancy Morning Sickness Worth Trying",
        "text_sha256": "8239afbd705cec0d2912f8a2c0ff276a22322a689b33c07f445d8e3a62d18039",
        "word_count": 9
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000001",
        "block_index": 1,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Light copy updates, updates to sourcing, and fact-checked for accuracy.",
        "text_sha256": "ce4b0fa95b50aecf6e7b67e3e57fba87415f35177add6e78e3c831eddc829533",
        "word_count": 10
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000002",
        "block_index": 2,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "morning sickness",
        "text_sha256": "4554a5c92d2ee3a617d100695770a34cbb083c3fb86694afec42173a8e43a933",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000003",
        "block_index": 3,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Struggling with morning sickness? Moms in the What to Expect Community share their best home remedies for pregnancy nausea.",
        "text_sha256": "58178b5e06383696c1b4db0dc610fdf18b4e8ebd842b748c6a00be8a17f344ec",
        "word_count": 19
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000004",
        "block_index": 4,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Feeling nauseous? You're not alone. Morning sickness affects an estimated 75% of moms-to-be Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, National Library of MedicineQuantifying the global rates of nausea and vomiting of pregnancy: a meta analysisSee All Sources [1] and can linger until week 16 of pregnancy (and for those who have a more severe form of morning sickness called hyperemesis gravidarum, even longer).",
        "text_sha256": "b23e1e57e28aa9fd42b90ba69aff38623d36bd8231a2ace14140c3253a744873",
        "word_count": 62
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000005",
        "block_index": 5,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceNational Institutes of Health, National Library of MedicineQuantifying the global rates of nausea and vomiting of pregnancy: a meta analysisSee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "dc701d9193cb1b12c64ee5971cf0b0cac01f554333db851692101bef31286e6a",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000006",
        "block_index": 6,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "And chances are, you might not have realized until you became pregnant that morning sickness isn't exclusive to the morning. It can strike any time of day — and sometimes all day. Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsMorning Sickness: Nausea and Vomiting of PregnancySee All Sources [2]",
        "text_sha256": "b2fe26ee9fe1d8b5c864f5015fe90308a32f5b69533204c2d158d7dad806c5a3",
        "word_count": 48
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000007",
        "block_index": 7,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Trusted SourceAmerican College of Obstetricians and GynecologistsMorning Sickness: Nausea and Vomiting of PregnancySee All Sources",
        "text_sha256": "3f3fa9d89c9fac148c59feb0529bf1a2d26e8a6a09a75a4011c12b9116977f47",
        "word_count": 15
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000008",
        "block_index": 8,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "There are ways to find relief, though. Below, moms in the What to Expect Community share their best morning sickness home remedies that are worth trying.",
        "text_sha256": "227574610220c3ff1148cf3b3b87025d2c86b80fdaf8785ecaad609a9b4b608e",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000009",
        "block_index": 9,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h2",
        "text": "Key Takeaways",
        "text_sha256": "cc3f7f0f4513969e418b56fb93ec0876fd96dd6498395b04301f70dbddff8a45",
        "word_count": 2
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000010",
        "block_index": 10,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Morning sickness is common and can strike anytime, affecting most pregnant women up to week 16 (or longer with severe cases like hyperemesis gravidarum).",
        "text_sha256": "ef64759d6a359e5087d52bc5e28c788db29340fa89e0f8974bbf6b795db49351",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000011",
        "block_index": 11,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "Simple home remedies can help, such as eating small, frequent meals; trying ginger, mint, lemon, or pickles; wearing Sea-Bands; and adjusting when you take prenatal vitamins.",
        "text_sha256": "5c2421c673e04d75dfd36111c2219f1879cc35b65bc76e391ec213ef7c1ecbfb",
        "word_count": 26
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000012",
        "block_index": 12,
        "block_type": "li",
        "tag": "li",
        "text": "If symptoms persist, options like acupuncture, vitamin B6, or prescription medication may provide relief — always with your doctor’s guidance.",
        "text_sha256": "bba90e2de133ec9b79afc46a0c0eb223eec17c442cb1776941da6cf031707463",
        "word_count": 20
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000013",
        "block_index": 13,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "1. Eat small meals throughout the day",
        "text_sha256": "9dc5670b2d2bf0d1d2790260d963ec33d1f3497fdd4a29b5686d84989d8edbcb",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000014",
        "block_index": 14,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Keeping meals frequent and small may help keep nausea at bay. \"Try nibbling crackers all day in tiny portions,\" says What to Expect Community member Jmoba. \"Also have proteins and fats like nuts and cheese.\"",
        "text_sha256": "a4de24dde1a7aead3440c623d7b28398a382cfe86509aa7021906406e44ee388",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000015",
        "block_index": 15,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Other ideas: Snack on peanut butter, yogurt, or chia pudding, or sip on smoothies made with yogurt to sneak in some extra protein.",
        "text_sha256": "76522c57ba464499a5d3be6003b79ebfb2d2cfab8b3b605119a60a9b0f61c43e",
        "word_count": 23
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000016",
        "block_index": 16,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "2. Embrace ginger",
        "text_sha256": "d90306814516082007653dc729d3136a4dd55c5cbea064dd89f79cffc6154ecb",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000017",
        "block_index": 17,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Ginger chews and ginger ale!\" says What to Expect Community member lguy. Many moms-to-be say ginger helps settle their stomachs, so try cooking with it, snacking on sweet ginger snacks, or even just smelling fresh ginger (or ginger essential oils) for a little relief.",
        "text_sha256": "20c06397a851f89d08fb63f8e0cb33b8bdef3e36d1043c8b0703a1e9aa9e2412",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000018",
        "block_index": 18,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "3. Go minty",
        "text_sha256": "3c26cff4ea6490fa90233926c2dae6aa9b274574d28db660b51810d94107cdd8",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000019",
        "block_index": 19,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Try chewing some mint gum when you start to feel nauseous,\" says What to Expect Community user Monica0328. \"It worked for me and some other girls I know.\"",
        "text_sha256": "72dd5a25c2b9853fd327123ebf5775969ab6a251c0c574bf2d275a6fbc1cf149",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000020",
        "block_index": 20,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Like ginger, mint can be a soothing option. In addition to gum, you can try smelling some mint leaves or mint-scented oils, or sprinkling some mint leaves into your water bottle.",
        "text_sha256": "1cb0b1b7fb8788328cbdd7d41d327521289ad41d207437d9a0d3cd3e07c0597e",
        "word_count": 31
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000021",
        "block_index": 21,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "4. Stock up on Sea-Bands",
        "text_sha256": "e7b7ee14f8a7a8b5185b6986d25980aef52ac18c87ccc6bd32286bc073aa2536",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000022",
        "block_index": 22,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "These 1-inch bands are widely available at drug and health food stores and may ease nausea by putting pressure on an acupressure point in the inner wrist. \"I'm nauseous all day, and so far, these have helped,\" says What to Expect Community parent fazi6566.",
        "text_sha256": "f1d22cf4e72f641c23b454642af3dfab9d724f0d83f93e76b296be935dde7b62",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000023",
        "block_index": 23,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "5. Add lemon to your water",
        "text_sha256": "a9456185ce344f4e5025b3da5c8f2b43c1fb5bc51ffb12f5dea53fac2609a10a",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000024",
        "block_index": 24,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Citrus fruits like lemon, lime, and orange have long been recommended for upset stomachs, and pregnancy is no exception. \"If I drink water on an empty stomach I throw up,\" says What to Expect Community user Murran13. \"I have been adding Minute Maid Lemonade Concentrate to mine — just enough so that I can handle it.\"",
        "text_sha256": "2eafcd49d351666cefea72e1b20da015ab6ef3f002c90402de8f399be617301c",
        "word_count": 56
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000025",
        "block_index": 25,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "You can also add slices of citrus to your water and eat foods with high water content like watermelon and citrus fruits.",
        "text_sha256": "463753205bb3dab761a4aac8757c16289b1e7a570005acbd9c1f10f2ea14c0c3",
        "word_count": 22
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000026",
        "block_index": 26,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "6. Snack on some pickles",
        "text_sha256": "3602532a132a0fa6b07b5c8ed2c2b210e929a20ba96ff743aaae2eb9d3b22377",
        "word_count": 5
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000027",
        "block_index": 27,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "It might sound strange, but several moms-to-be in the What to Expect Community swear by this trick: \"Pickles! And the juice. I know it sounds completely opposite of what you want to eat when you're feeling nauseous, but they helped me so much!\" One mom-to-be said even just the smell of pickles could give her some relief.",
        "text_sha256": "2e4d7d2b66032e80916e95c3595bd212ff7853bb916c141907a6ac07b83ffe77",
        "word_count": 57
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000028",
        "block_index": 28,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "7. Try Pedialyte",
        "text_sha256": "c37a1370d838a8dd8079dd82018ad0224f6cb24046cf3ef0c492d5c21bb58645",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000029",
        "block_index": 29,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Hydration is key, but if you're struggling to keep down water, many moms-to-be swear by Pedialyte. \"Having a Pedialyte popsicle first thing in the morning has helped,\" says What to Expect Community user ahathaway173. \"I get some hydration and electrolytes without actually drinking anything.\"",
        "text_sha256": "d0213677d477c7802819b54bb0f35e5e546bce00cbf0216bcba99d6f371c3c16",
        "word_count": 44
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000030",
        "block_index": 30,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Pedialyte. \"Having a Pedialyte popsicle first thing in the morning has helped,\" says What to Expect Community user ahathaway173. \"I get some hydration and electrolytes without actually drinking anything.\"",
        "text_sha256": "e981f48ae26eb3729c6581b0ca5056ade70b9edfd127a88c965b227a99479fbc",
        "word_count": 29
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000031",
        "block_index": 31,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Turning them into popsicles is as easy pouring it into an ice tray or popsicle mold and freezing. The coolness of an ice pop is soothing and doesn’t require you to chew or sip to get hydrated.",
        "text_sha256": "1d833a68088f1e2e0bad9ee9d2ece6b0135a0b497071628e15e82c23b990d716",
        "word_count": 37
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000032",
        "block_index": 32,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Struggling with morning sickness? Open the What to Expect app for more ways to manage pregnancy nausea, plus a week-by-week guide to other symptoms you may be experiencing.",
        "text_sha256": "4f0f1285e39a885d1be088e72b7f5e57d457dcf0e643da044ba06b68247a73cf",
        "word_count": 28
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000033",
        "block_index": 33,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "8. Consider the timing of your prenatal vitamin",
        "text_sha256": "6f85379b7389f59242cab2fcb5a1ce62a2a2981101ed55d9d52f17ae7796b94b",
        "word_count": 8
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000034",
        "block_index": 34,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Some moms-to-be find that taking their prenatal vitamin at a different time of day (\"I noticed a HUGE difference when I switched to taking my prenatal vitamins right before bed,\" says What to Expect Community user mrsjmscharer), taking it on a full stomach, or asking their practitioner to recommend an alternate formula can help.",
        "text_sha256": "096f01c58fd56a6fb667fa635132310eb2606e9fd4f416ead8db902b6ed1b37b",
        "word_count": 54
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000035",
        "block_index": 35,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "9. Make a batch of pregnancy popsicles",
        "text_sha256": "25a46d0eb84098195560b6386f611b01545b50db8b82c17d50f3fc27e4303474",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000036",
        "block_index": 36,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"I ate popsicles like they were being eradicated!\" says What to Expect Community member mrsjmschare. \"I had popsicles morning, noon, and night. It was the only thing I could keep down and really helped me.\"",
        "text_sha256": "2e049c7e2f85e4b44c4e0b00cac5829da79ea39295dd814401b5243e05d36c50",
        "word_count": 35
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000037",
        "block_index": 37,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "This tip makes sense: Popsicles are sweet and hydrating, making them a perfect choice for nauseous moms-to-be. Look for store-bought brands (or make your own) that contain tummy soothers like ginger or mint.",
        "text_sha256": "50a241ab617e456a27d2ceaa11ca50c022070c65398891f16c567c1f8fa41d22",
        "word_count": 33
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000038",
        "block_index": 38,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "10. Consider acupuncture",
        "text_sha256": "ca0c813cf19405b4453409ffa7347bc58e4291fb8152a3272e87845347125213",
        "word_count": 3
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000039",
        "block_index": 39,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "Some moms-to-be credit acupuncture with helping to ease morning sickness along with other pregnancy symptoms like heartburn and sciatica . \"I started to feel better because I went to acupuncture,\" says What to Expect Community user virper. \"I am really happy I did ... it can be a good option.\"",
        "text_sha256": "1cffa4d012afda8df7fe3faf736c95def97346f5f5def45d2f069b79fdd1ba5d",
        "word_count": 50
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000040",
        "block_index": 40,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "In fact, some studies have shown that acupuncture that targets the wrist may help reduce nausea and vomiting associated with morning sickness (though other studies have not found the same effect). Trusted SourceAmerican Journal of Obstetrics and GynecologyAcupressure and acustimulation bands for control of nausea: A brief reviewSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "27bbbae8a70586d9adcff975513554ca1e8cf6e1e30e2bc329dc5ff688c3bf01",
        "word_count": 51
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000041",
        "block_index": 41,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "ome studies have shown that acupuncture that targets the wrist may help reduce nausea and vomiting associated with morning sickness (though other studies have not found the same effect). Trusted SourceAmerican Journal of Obstetrics and GynecologyAcupressure and acustimulation bands for control of nausea: A brief reviewSee All Sources [3]",
        "text_sha256": "ad3c0640ddb8ca9ebcb947951d366152c40fbc6db9f62955deddf22f364ce439",
        "word_count": 49
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000042",
        "block_index": 42,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "11. Ask your doctor about supplements",
        "text_sha256": "5015a881f43ccab41e2f81c772042052fbc9077906f100272dcd3cb3a5c02a7c",
        "word_count": 6
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000043",
        "block_index": 43,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If your morning sickness isn't responding to other remedies, your practitioner may recommend taking an additional vitamin B6 supplement or the antihistamine doxylamine (found in Unisom SleepTabs). \"This has saved me and made it possible for me to work,\" says What to Expect Community user laurakbon.",
        "text_sha256": "675cc620dc70b345d4e29dab5c5e6fd32bab43f4f6d21c90b4297f14d7609237",
        "word_count": 46
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000044",
        "block_index": 44,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "However, never test these supplements (or any other traditional or herbal medication for morning sickness) without first getting the green light from your doctor.",
        "text_sha256": "fe7df22b704d705c94c34754b6dc65de3feae90bf440c2c52f0195ba1fabecfb",
        "word_count": 24
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000045",
        "block_index": 45,
        "block_type": "heading",
        "tag": "h3",
        "text": "12. Talk to your doctor about medication",
        "text_sha256": "bee8e3ba05160baaeeb706f2d130119d5cbd0fc836fab32f3e8fd02b008ecbf5",
        "word_count": 7
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000046",
        "block_index": 46,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "If you have severe symptoms and home remedies aren't helping, reach out to your practitioner for guidance. Your doctor may recommend a prescription drug such as Diclegis that's been approved by the FDA to treat nausea and vomiting during pregnancy .",
        "text_sha256": "29ed0d824a712d3cbbc846fbc441ffa97a32708296789dcd41c57bc8d55dc735",
        "word_count": 41
      },
      {
        "block_id": "block_000047",
        "block_index": 47,
        "block_type": "p",
        "tag": "p",
        "text": "\"Don't be afraid to call your doctor's office and ask for a prescription,\" says What to Expect Community user twinzies2017. \"It was the only thing that helped me get out of bed in the mornings.\"",
        "text_sha256": "2bb09583f4d8faac97bed5c3af7939458659f94472408da387c58d5e73cc375a",
        "word_count": 35
      },
